{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/healthcareapis/fhir-converter","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:11.770Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/healthcareapis/fhir-converter/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/healthcareapis/fhir-converter/about"},"readme":"## About\n\nFHIR converter enables conversion of health data from legacy formats to and from FHIR using the [Liquid templating language](https://shopify.github.io/liquid/) and the .NET runtime.\n\nThis container image provides ready-to-use REST based APIs that support the following conversions: **HL7v2 to FHIR**, **C-CDA to FHIR**, **JSON to FHIR**, **FHIR STU3 to R4**, and **FHIR to HL7v2**(Preview).\n\nPlease refer to the FHIR converter official GitHub [repository](https://github.com/microsoft/FHIR-Converter) for more information.\n\n## Featured Tags\n\n`docker pull mcr.microsoft.com/healthcareapis/fhir-converter`\n\nList of all available tags can be found [here](https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/healthcareapis/fhir-converter/tags).\n\n## Usage\n\nFor detailed instructions on how to use this container, and configure a FHIR converter service using this container image, please refer to the [setup instructions](https://github.com/microsoft/FHIR-Converter/blob/main/docs/how-to-guides/setup-convert-service.md) on Github.\n\n## Support\n\nFor support, feedback or general questions, please open an [issue](https://github.com/microsoft/FHIR-Converter/labels/mcr-fhir-converter).\n\n## License\n\n- Legal Notice: [MAR Legal Notice](https://github.com/microsoft/containerregistry/blob/main/legal/Container-Images-Legal-Notice.md)\n\nThe project is covered by MIT License. The detailed license text is available [here](https://github.com/microsoft/FHIR-Converter/blob/main/LICENSE).","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered"